 "final_passage": "Corbel's average zero-shot nDCG@10 gain over Dovetail-DR, the same bi-encoder trained with standard in-batch negatives, was 4.7 points (40.7 vs 36.0), slightly smaller than the 5.2-point improvement previously reported for denoised hard-negative mining on a biomedical collection. Corbel outperformed Dovetail-DR on all four held-out collections, with per-collection gains ranging from 3.8 points on Felloe-Fin (35.0 vs 31.2) to 5.9 points on Moorstone-Bio (50.6 vs 44.7). Corbel also exceeded the lexical reference Lexi-Sparse on average (40.7 vs 35.3) and on every collection, with the largest margin on Felloe-Fin (35.0 vs 27.9, +7.1 points).",
